      <description>On November 26, 2025, Hong Kong firefighters were called to Wang Fuk Court, a complex of eight 31-story residential towers. What followed was the city’s deadliest fire in almost eight decades, an inferno that claimed 168 lives and triggered a year of recriminations over who was at fault. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
